y, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{c} \\times (3 \\mathbf{a} - 2 \\mathbf{b}) = 3 (\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{a}) - 2 (\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{b})\n\\]\n\nWe know that \\(\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{a} = -(\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{c})\\) and \\(\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{b} = -(\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c})\\). Using the given vectors, we can substitute these into our equation:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{a} = -\\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -4 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{b} = -\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 18 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -18 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nNow substitute these into the expression \\(3 (\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{a}) - 2 (\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{b})\\):\n\n\\[\n3 \\begin{pmatrix} -4 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix} - 2 \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -18 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -12 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -6 \\end{pmatrix} - \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ 14 \\\\ -36 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -12 + 2 \\\\ -21 - 14 \\\\ -6 + 36 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -10 \\\\ -35 \\\\ 30 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} -10 \\\\ -35 \\\\ 30 \\end{pmatrix}}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} -10 \\\\ -35 \\\\ 30 \\end{pmatrix}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
